          %p
            on configuration space. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            of this line bundle – its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            – is hence the
            %em magnetic anomaly
            in higher gauge theory.
          %p
            \&amp;lbrack;cf.
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Freed00"} Freed 2002 (2.29)
          %p In the next section we formalize properly the notion of this line bundle on configuration space.
          %h3#the_anomaly_line_bundle The anomaly line bundle
          %p
            In order to formalize this we have to refine the formalization of the structure of the configuration space. So far we had regarded the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{dim X - n}_{diff}(X) \times H_{diff}^{n+1}(X)
            of gauge equivalence classes of field configurations. This is the set of connected components of the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^{dim X - n}_{diff}(X) \times C_{diff}^{n+1}(X)
                  \\in
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are field configurations on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                are
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                are gauge transformations of gauge transformation,
            %li
              %p and so on.
          %p
            Moreover, this cocycle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            is not just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
            but it naturally has
            %em smooth structure
            making it a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Conf
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi SmoothGrpd
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Conf
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\Big[
                  X
                  ,\,
                  \\big(
                  \\mathbf{B}^{n}U(1)
                  \\times
                  \\mathbf{B}^{dim X - n-1}U(1)
                  \\big)_{conn}
                  \\Big]
                  \\;\in\;
                  SmoothGrpd_{\infty}
          %p
            for this smooth
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            in terms of the
            %a{:href => "infinity1-topos#ClosedMonoidalStructure"} closed monoidal structure on the (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi SmoothMfd
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow Smooth\infty Grpd
            into the target object of the higher
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid#StrucDifferentialCohomology"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            of sheaves on
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
          %p
            This smooth structure is characterized by saying that for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
            the
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Conf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi diff
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Conf(U)
                  \\simeq
                  C^{dim X - n}_{diff}(U \times X) \times C_{diff}^{n+1}(U \times X )
          %p
            of gauge fields on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with the parameter space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
            for details on how differential forms on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ×
